  "slug": "colored-indexes-832d",
  "summary": "Recent preprints apply compressed-space indexes to terabase assemblies, long reads, and haplotype selection, with several reporting speedups over existing tools.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is compressed, sequence-aware indexing for exact matching over large genomic collections. A BWT run-length index yields SMEMs and MEMs across terabase pangenome assemblies in compressed space and sublinear time. Move structures give matching statistics and SMEMs in compressed space, with reported speedups over PHONI and ropebwt3. Genomic tessellations pair a canonical quasi-periodic DNA factorization with a tessellated BWT index for faster long-read mapping. SIFT applies closed-syncmer parsing and pseudo-MEM queries to select reference haplotypes for T2T patching with ImpuT2T. What is new is exact-match computation at pangenome scale within compressed space, and index-driven haplotype selection for T2T genome patching. Infernal-GPU, which parallelizes covariance-model dynamic programming on GPUs and recalibrates Rfam E-values, addresses a different problem and is not part of this thread.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-18"
}
